        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0001442</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A quantitative confidence value that measures the minimum false discovery rate that is incurred when calling that test significant. 
To compute q-values, it is necessary to know the p-value produced by a test and possibly set a false discovery rate level.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
