        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0200094</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A logarithmic transformation is a data transformation consisting in the application of the logarithm function with a given base a (where a&gt;0 and a is not equal to 1) to a (one dimensional) positive real number input. The logarithm function with base a can be defined as the inverse of the exponential function with the same base. See e.g. http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Logarithm.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
