        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0500006</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A parallel group design or independent measure design is a study design which uses unique experimental unit each experimental group, in other word no two individuals are shared between experimental groups, hence also known as parallel group design. Subjects of a treatment group receive a unique combination of independent variable values making up a treatment</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
