        <Literal xml:lang="en">The studentized range (q) distribution is a probability distribution used by the Tukey Honestly Significant Difference test. 

The distribution of the statistic
[x̄(k)- x̄(1)]/(s/√n)
where random samples of size n have been taken from k independent and identically distributed normal populations, with x̄(1) and x̄(k) being, respectively, the smallest and largest of the k sample means, and s2 being the pooled estimate of the common variance. This statistic is particularly used in multiple comparison tests.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
