        <Literal xml:lang="en">Hardy-Weinberg equilibrium hypothesis is a good of fit hypothesis which states that allele and genotype frequencies in a population will remain constant from generation to generation in the absence of other evolutionary influences (non-random mating, mutation, selection, genetic drift, gene flow and meiotic drive).</Literal>
