        <Literal xml:lang="en">the Brown Forsythe test is a statistical test which evaluates if the variance of different groups are equal. It relies on computing the median rather than the mean, as used in the Levene&apos;s test for homoschedacity.
This test maybe used to, for instance, ensure that the conditions of applications of ANOVA are met.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
