        <Literal xml:lang="en">The Kruskal–Wallis test is a null hypothesis statistical testing objective which  allows multiple (n&gt;=2) groups (or conditions or treatments) to be compared, without making the assumption that values are normally distributed. The Kruskal–Wallis test is the non-parametric equivalent of the independent samples ANOVA.
The Kruskal–Wallis test is most commonly used when there is one nominal variable and one measurement variable, and the measurement variable does not meet the normality assumption of an anova.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
