        <Literal xml:lang="en">the Scheffe test is a data transformation which evaluates all possible contrasts and adjusting the levels significance by accounting for multiple comparison. The test is therefore conservative. Confidence intervals can be constructed for the corresponding linear regression.  It was developped by  American statistician Henry  Scheffe in 1959.</Literal>
