        <Literal xml:lang="en">Threshold cycle (or Ct or Cq) is a count which is defined as the fractional PCR cycle number at which the reporter fluorescence is greater than the threshold in the context of the RT-qPCR assay. The Ct is a basic principle of real time PCR and is an essential component in producing accurate and reproducible data.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
