        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000199</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">the Mauchly&apos;s test for sphericity is a statistical test which evaluates if the variance of the differences between all combinations of the groups are equal, a property known as &apos;sphericity&apos; in the context of repeated measures. It is used for instance prior to repeated measure ANOVA.
The test works by assessing if a Wishart-distributed covariance matrix (or transformation thereof) is proportional to a given matrix.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000199</IRI>
        <Literal>Alejandra Gonzalez-Beltran</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
