        <Literal xml:lang="en">Bayes factor is a ratio between 2 probabilities of observing data according 2 distinct models. It is used in Bayes model selection to evaluate which model best explains the data. if K&lt;0, the model used in the denominator term is supported, if K&gt;1, the model used in the numerator term is supported.
The Bayes factor is about the plausibility of 2 different models</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
