        <Literal xml:lang="en">The Michaelis constant  is the substrate concentration at which the reaction rate is at half-maximum, and is an inverse measure of the substrate&apos;s affinity for the enzyme—as a small  indicates high affinity, meaning that the rate will approach  more quickly.[5] The value of  is dependent on both the enzyme and the substrate, as well as conditions such as temperature and pH.</Literal>
