        <Literal xml:lang="en">negative binomial probability distribution is a discrete probability distribution of the number of successes in a sequence of Bernoulli trials before a specified (non-random) number of failures (denoted r) occur. The negative binomial distribution, also known as the Pascal distribution or Pólya distribution, gives the probability of  r-1 successes and x  failures in x+r-1 trials, and success on the (x+r)th trial.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
