        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000313</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Plackett-Burman design is a type of study design optimizing multifactorial experiments characterized by their parsimony  and economy  with the run number a multiple of 4 (rather than a power of 2). 
Plackett-Burman design is often used for screening experiments where the main effect is often heavily confounded with two-factor interactions.
This type of design is very useful for economically detecting large main effects, assuming all interactions are negligible when compared with the few important main effects.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117"/>
