        <Literal xml:lang="en">root-mean-square standardized effect is a statistic which denotes effect size in the context of analysis of variance and corresponds to the square root of the arithmetic average of p  standardized effects  (effects normalized to be expressed in standard deviation units).</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
