        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000382</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">&apos;has order in sequence&apos; is a special case of the &apos;is about&apos; relation being used to be able to enumerate the different terms within a linear mixed model formula (thus assinging and order to random effect terms, fixed effect terms, interaction effect terms and error terms).</Literal>
