        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000433</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">McNemar&apos;s test is a statistical test used on paired nominal data. It is applied to 2 × 2 contingency tables with a dichotomous trait, with matched pairs of subjects, to determine whether the row and column marginal frequencies are equal (that is, whether there is &quot;marginal homogeneity&quot;). It is named after Quinn McNemar, who introduced it in 1947.
An application of the test in genetics is the transmission disequilibrium test for detecting linkage disequilibrium</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000433</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Philippe Rocca-Serra</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000433</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">McNemar&apos;s Chi-squared Test for Count Data</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
