        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000434</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Cochran&apos;s Q test is a statistical test used for unreplicated randomized block design experiments with a binary response variable and paired data.
In the analysis of two-way randomized block designs where the response variable can take only two possible outcomes (coded as 0 and 1), Cochran&apos;s Q test is a non-parametric statistical test to verify whether k treatments have identical effects.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117"/>
