        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000459</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">group sequential design is a study design used in clinical trial settings in which interim analyses of the data are conducted after groups of patients are recruited. After each interim analysis, the trial may stop early if the evidence so far shows the new treatment is particularly effective or ineffective. Such designs are ethical and cost-effective, and so are of great interest in practice.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000459</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Philippe Rocca-Serra</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000459</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">adapted from https://www.jstatsoft.org/article/view/v066i02/v66i02.pdf</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000041"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000459</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/gsDesign/index.html</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000459</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">group sequential design</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000460</IRI>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122</IRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000460</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">interim analysis is a data transformation used to analyzed studies implementing a group-sequential design, to evaluate and  interpret the accumulating information during a clinical trial. It means that the analysis of data that is conducted before full data collection has been completed. Clinical trials are unusual in that enrollment of patients is a continual process staggered in time. This means that if a treatment is particularly beneficial or harmful compared to the concurrent placebo group while the study is on-going, the investigators are ethically obliged to assess that difference using the data at hand and to make a deliberate consideration of terminating the study earlier than planned.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000460</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Philippe Rocca-Serra</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000460</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">adapted from https://onlinecourses.science.psu.edu/stat509/node/75
and from wikipedia:
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interim_analysis

last accessed: 2017-10-9</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000041"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000460</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en"></Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000391"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000460</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en"></Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
