        <Literal xml:lang="en">Satterthwaite degree of freedom approximation is a type of degree of freedom approximation which is used to estimate an “effective degrees of freedom” for a probability distribution formed from several independent normal distributions where only estimates of the variance are known. It was originally developed by statistician Franklin E. Satterthwaite.</Literal>
