        <Literal xml:lang="en">an additive genetic model is a data item which refer to the contributions to the final phenotype from more than one gene, or from alleles of a single gene (in heterozygotes), that combine in such a way that the sum of their effects in unison is equal to the sum of their individual effects and their dominance effect (of alleles at a single locus).</Literal>
