        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000041"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000525</IRI>
        <Literal></Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000525</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">covariance matrix</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000526</IRI>
        <Literal>https://www.r-bloggers.com/setup-up-the-inverse-of-additive-relationship-matrix-in-r/</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000526</IRI>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122</IRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000526</IRI>
        <Literal>the numerator relationship matrix is the matrix of *expected* additive genetic relationships between individuals. This matrix was originally used by Henderson (Henderson, C.R. 1976. A simple method for computing the inverse of a numerator relationship matrix used in prediction of breeding values. Biometrics 32:69-83.) to account for covariances between random effects, and therefore to use information from relatives in estimation of breeding value. Among the properties of the NRM matrix (also known as the A matrix), it is symmetric, the diagonal value correspond to 1+ the inbreeding coefficient for an individual.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000526</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Philippe Rocca-Serra</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000526</IRI>
        <Literal>A matrix</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000526</IRI>
        <Literal>adapted from:
https://jvanderw.une.edu.au/Genetic_properties_of_the_animal_model.pdf
and from:
Henderson, C.R. 1976. A simple method for computing the inverse of a numerator relationship matrix used in prediction of breeding values. Biometrics 32:69-83.
https://doi.org/10.2307/2529339</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000032"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000526</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">NRM</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000041"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000526</IRI>
        <Literal>https://rdrr.io/cran/sommer/man/A.mat.html</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000526</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">numerator relationship matrix</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000527</IRI>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122</IRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000527</IRI>
        <Literal>The degree of freedom denominator is the number of degrees of freedom that the estimate of variance used in the denominator is based on. It is one of the parameters for the F-distribution used to compute probabilities in analysis of variance.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000527</IRI>
        <Literal>term request:
https://github.com/ISA-tools/stato/issues/71</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000527</IRI>
        <Literal>Hanna Cwiek</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000527</IRI>
        <Literal>Philippe Rocca-Serra</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000032"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000527</IRI>
        <Literal>den df</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000032"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000527</IRI>
        <Literal>df2</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000527</IRI>
        <Literal>denominator degrees of freedom</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000528</IRI>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122</IRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000528</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A matrix of relationships among a group of individuals, which can be used to predict breeding values, to manage inbreeding and in genetic conservation. It can be calculated from the pedigree, but it is also possible to calculate the relationship matrix from genotypes at genetic markers such as single-nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs). Elements of the genomic relationship matrix are estimates of the realized proportion of the genome that two individuals share, whereas the pedigree-derived relationship matrix is the expectation of this proportion.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000528</IRI>
        <Literal>Philippe Rocca-Serra</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000528</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">https://doi.org/10.3168/jds.2007-0980</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000528</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/22059574</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000032"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000528</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">realized genomic relationship matrix</Literal>
