        <Literal xml:lang="en">a Bayesian model is a statistical model  where inference is based on using Bayes theorem to obtain a posterior distribution for a quantity (or quantities) of interest for some model (such as parameter values) based on some prior distribution for the relevant unknown parameters and the likelihood from the model.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
