        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000531</IRI>
        <Literal>a prior probability distribution is a probability distribution used as input to a Bayesian model to represent a priori knowledge about a model parameter. Along with the acquired/observed data, it is used to compute a posterior distribution according to the Bayes theorem.</Literal>
