        <Literal>Bayes C pi is a data transformation used to compute estimated breeding values using a Bayesian model and which assesses the SNP effect using MonteCarlo Markov chain methods. Bayes C pi treats the prior probability π that a SNP has zero effect as unknown.
The method was devised to address short comings of Bayes A and Bayes B approaches</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
