        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000587</IRI>
        <Literal>the percentage of variance is an output of principal component analysis (PCRA), which is obtained by forming the ratio of an eigen-value divided by the sum of all eigen-values. This produces a &quot;percentage of variance&quot; for each eigen-vector.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
