        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000590</IRI>
        <Literal>median of the ratios corrected count is kind of count produced during an  RNA-Seq data normalization procedure which corresponds to dividing  counts  by sample-specific size factors determined by median ratio of gene counts relative to geometric mean per gene.
It was first described by Anders and Huber in 2010 (https://doi.org/10.1186/gb-2010-11-10-r106)


Recommended use:

-&quot;median of the ratios corrected count&quot; is suited for Differential Expression analysis or between samples. 

-&quot;median of the ratios corrected count&quot; is NOT suited for gene count comparisons within a sample.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
