    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000609</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">measure of hypothesis testing</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000610</IRI>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122</IRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000610</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">measure of association is a statistic which quantitatively represents a relationship between two or more variables</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000610</IRI>
        <Literal>Expert Working Group Agreement: 2022-03-16 vote 7-0 by Mario Tristan, Paola Rosati, Louis Leff, nisha mathew, Philippe Rocca-Serra, Harold Lehmann, Janice Tufte</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000610</IRI>
        <Literal>Brian S. Alper, Joanne Dehnbostel, Kenneth Wilkins, Muhammad Afzal, Neeraj Ojha</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000610</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">COKA group</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000610</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">measure of association</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000611</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">measure of correlation is a measure of association between ordinal or continuous variables.

A value of 0 means no association. 
A positive value means a positive association (as one variable increases, the other variable increases). 
A negative value means a negative association (as one variable increases, the other variable decreases).
For correlation coefficients, the possible values range from +1 (perfect positive association) to -1 (perfect negative association)</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000611</IRI>
        <Literal>Expert Working Group Agreement: 2022-11-16 vote 5-0 by Brian S. Alper, Philippe Rocca-Serra, Harold Lehman, Jesus Lopez-Alcalde, Eric Harvey</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000611</IRI>
        <Literal>Brian S. Alper, Joanne Dehnbostel, Muhammad Afzal, Yuan Gao, Kenneth Wilkins, Harold Lehmann</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000611</IRI>
        <Literal>correlation</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000611</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">COKA group</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000611</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">measure of correlation</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000612</IRI>
        <Literal>A measure of correlation, ranging from -1 to 1, that measures the strength and direction of the relationship between ranks by value of two ordinal or continuous variables, and is calculated based on the difference in the number of concordant and discordant pairs of rankings divided by the total number of pairs of rankings, where ties are not counted among the pairs of rankings.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000612</IRI>
        <Literal>Expert Working Group Agreement: 2023-01-25 vote 5-0 by Mario Tristan, Jesus Lopez-Alcalde, Joanne Dehnbostel,  Harold Lehmann, Eric Harvey</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000612</IRI>
        <Literal>Brian S. Alper, Harold Lehmann, Joanne Dehnbostel</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000612</IRI>
        <Literal>Goodman-Kruskal gamma</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000612</IRI>
        <Literal>gamma coefficient</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000612</IRI>
        <Literal>gamma statistic</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000612</IRI>
        <Literal>adapted from: https://stats.stackexchange.com/questions/18112/how-do-the-Goodman-Kruskal-gamma-and-the-Kendall-tau-or-Spearman-rho-correlation</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000612</IRI>
        <Literal>Goodman and Kruskal&apos;s gamma</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000613</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A statistic that is a subtraction of one quantity from another.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000613</IRI>
        <Literal>Expert Working Group Agreement: 2021-12-01 vote 5-0 by Philippe Rocca-Serra, Paola Rosati, Joanne Dehnbostel, Jesus Lopez-Alcalde, Janice Tufte</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000613</IRI>
        <Literal>Harold Lehmann, Brian S. Alper, Muhammad Afzal, Khalid Shahin, Philippe Rocca-Serra, Kenneth Wilkins, Joanne Dehnbostel, Janice Tufte</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000613</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">COKA group</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000613</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">difference</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000614</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A statistic that is a subtraction of one quantity from another, with no modification of the resulting value.

As a type of statistic, &quot;Absolute Difference&quot; is the actual difference between two quantities and can be positive or negative depending on the order of subtraction. The term &quot;Absolute Difference&quot; should not be confused with the mathematical term &apos;absolute value&apos; which is a numerical value without a negative sign.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000614</IRI>
        <Literal>Expert Working Group Agreement: 2021-12-01 vote 5-0 by Philippe Rocca-Serra, Paola Rosati, Joanne Dehnbostel, Jesus Lopez-Alcalde, Janice Tufte</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000614</IRI>
        <Literal>Brian S. Alper, Harold Lehmann, Kenneth Wilkins, Joanne Dehnbostel, Muhammad Afzal, Khalid Shahin, Janice Tufte</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000614</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">COKA/SEVCO group</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000614</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">absolute difference</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000615</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A statistic that is a difference between 1 and a ratio of the two quantities being compared.

Relative Difference = 1 - ( a / b ).   Because 1 - ( a / b ) is not equal to 1 - ( b / a ), Relative Difference may be expressed as &quot;Relative Difference with respect to b&quot; when referring to 1 - ( a / b ).


The relative difference can also be defined as a statistic that is a ratio of the absolute difference (of the two quantities being compared) to the reference value (one of the quantities being compared). Relative Difference = ( b - a ) / ( b ) where b is the reference value and this may also be called &quot;Relative Difference with respect to b&quot;.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000615</IRI>
        <Literal>Expert Working Group Agreement: 2022-06-29 vote 5-0 by Jesus Lopez-Alcalde, Philippe Rocca-Serra, Mario Tristan, Harold Lehmann, Eric Harvey</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000615</IRI>
        <Literal>Brian S. Alper, Muhammad Afzal, Kenneth Wilkins, Joanne Dehnbostel</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000615</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">COKA group</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000615</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">relative difference</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000616</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A statistic that is a subtraction of one count from another.

The term Count Difference is used to specify the Absolute Difference is with respect to a count or number of items (such as number of events, platelet counts, sample size e.g. number of people in the group) to distinguish from differences in other types of statistics (mean difference, median difference, risk difference, etc.)</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000616</IRI>
        <Literal></Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000616</IRI>
        <Literal>Expert Working Group Agreement: 2021-12-15 vote 6-0 by Robin Ann Yurk, Janice Tufte, Paola Rosati, Harold Lehmann, Joanne Dehnbostel, Muhammad Afzal</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000616</IRI>
        <Literal>Harold Lehmann, Brian S. Alper, Muhammad Afzal, Khalid Shahin, Philippe Rocca-Serra, Kenneth Wilkins, Joanne Dehnbostel, Janice Tufte</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000616</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">COKA group</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000616</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">count difference</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000617</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A difference that is a subtraction of one median from another.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000617</IRI>
        <Literal>Expert Working Group Agreement: 2021-12-01 vote 6-0 by Philippe Rocca-Serra, Paola Rosati, Robin Ann Yurk, Joanne Dehnbostel, Jesus Lopez-Alcalde, Janice Tufte</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000617</IRI>
        <Literal>Brian S. Alper, Harold Lehmann, Joanne Dehnbostel, Khalid Shahin, Janice Tufte, Muhammad Afzal, Kenneth Wilkins</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000617</IRI>
        <Literal>difference in median</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000617</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">COKA group</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000617</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">median difference</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000618</IRI>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122</IRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000618</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A standardized mean difference which is calculated as a difference between two means, divided by a square root of an average of the variances of the two groups.

In Cohen&apos;s d statistic, the statistical measure of dispersion is specified as the square root of an average of the variances of the two groups being compared. The variances of the two groups are based on within-group standard deviations.

For sample sizes &lt; 50, a correction factor is used.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000618</IRI>
        <Literal>Expert Working Group Agreement: 2022-07-20 vote 5-0 by Philippe Rocca-Serra, Mario Tristan, Jesus Lopez-Alcalde, Harold Lehmann, Eric Harvey</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117"/>
