        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000618</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Cohen&apos;s d</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000619</IRI>
        <Literal></Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000619</IRI>
        <Literal>A proportion in which the numerator represents the correctly non-detected items within the denominator that represents all items not detected.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000619</IRI>
        <Literal>Expert Working Group Agreement: 2022-01-26 vote 8-0 by Robin Ann Yurk, Janice Tufte, Harold Lehmann, Philippe Rocca-Serra, Paola Rosati, Mario Tristan, Brian S. Alper, Jesus Lopez-Alcalde</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000619</IRI>
        <Literal>In a population of people with and without a disease, and a test which is positive (suggesting the disease) or negative (suggesting not having the disease), the negative predictive value is the proportion of true negatives (all people without the disease who test negative) within all the people with a negative test (true negatives plus false negatives). NPV = TN / (TN + FN).</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000619</IRI>
        <Literal>Harold Lehmann, Ken Wilkins, Philippe Rocca-Serra, Joanne Dehnbostel</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000619</IRI>
        <Literal>COKA/SEVCO</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000619</IRI>
        <Literal>negative predictive value</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000620</IRI>
        <Literal>A proportion in which the numerator represents the cases in which an event or characteristic occurs and the denominator represents all possible cases.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000620</IRI>
        <Literal>Expert Working Group Agreement: 2022-06-29 vote 6-0 by Jesus Lopez-Alcalde, Philippe Rocca-Serra, Mario Tristan, Janice Tufte, Harold Lehmann, Eric Harvey</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000620</IRI>
        <Literal>In the English language, &apos;risk&apos; may be used synonymously with &apos;hazard&apos;, &apos;chance&apos;, &apos;likelihood&apos;, &apos;relative likelihood&apos;, &apos;probability&apos; and many other terms. In SEVCO the term &apos;risk&apos; is explicitly defined for how it is used in other terms such as &apos;Risk Ratio&apos; and &apos;Relative Risk Difference&apos;  The statistical definition of &apos;risk&apos; does not have a negative or undesirable connotation.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000620</IRI>
        <Literal>Brian S. Alper, Harold Lehmann, Joanne Dehnbostel, Muhammad Afzal, Janice Tufte</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000620</IRI>
        <Literal>COKA/SEVCO</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000620</IRI>
        <Literal>risk</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000621</IRI>
        <Literal>diagnostic yield is a proportion in which the numerator represents the correctly detected items within the denominator that represents all items tested.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000621</IRI>
        <Literal>2022-08-10 vote 5-0 by Philippe Rocca-Serra, Mario Tristan, Harold Lehmann, Eric Harvey, Paola Rosati</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000621</IRI>
        <Literal>Brian S. Alper, Harold Lehmann, Joanne Dehnbostel, Kenneth Wilkins</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000621</IRI>
        <Literal>&quot;Diagnostic yield was defined as the number of participants with positive findings for advanced neoplasia relative to all participants&quot; in https://pubs.rsna.org/doi/10.1148/radiol.12112486
Other &apos;definitions&apos; found include synonymous use with sensitivity, and &apos;diagnostic yield&apos; describing the statistic array of TP, FP, TN, and FN data.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
