        <Literal>Expert Working Group Agreement: 2022-07-20 vote 5-0 by Philippe Rocca-Serra, Mario Tristan, Jesus Lopez-Alcalde, Harold Lehmann, Eric Harvey</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000634</IRI>
        <Literal>Brian S. Alper, Harold Lehmann, Joanne Dehnbostel</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000634</IRI>
        <Literal>COKA/SEVCO</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000634</IRI>
        <Literal>reciprocal of difference</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000635</IRI>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428</IRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000635</IRI>
        <Literal>A statistic that represents the number of units that needs to be treated to prevent one additional undesired outcome. The Number Needed to Treat is calculated as the reciprocal of a treatment effect estimate, where the effect estimate is expressed as a risk difference.

The Number Needed to Treat (NNT) value is often rounded up to the next highest whole integer</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000635</IRI>
        <Literal>Expert Working Group Agreement: 2022-07-20 vote 7-0 by Cauê Monaco, Janice Tufte, Philippe Rocca-Serra, Mario Tristan, Jesus Lopez-Alcalde, Harold Lehmann, Eric Harvey</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000635</IRI>
        <Literal>Brian S. Alper, Harold Lehmann, Joanne Dehnbostel, Kenneth Wilkins, Janice Tufte</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000635</IRI>
        <Literal>NTT</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000635</IRI>
        <Literal>NTTB</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000635</IRI>
        <Literal>number needed to treat to benefit</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000635</IRI>
        <Literal>COKA/SEVCO</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000635</IRI>
        <Literal>number needed to treat</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000636</IRI>
        <Literal>Number needed to screen was then calculated by dividing the number needed to treat for treating risk factors by the prevalence of disease that was unrecognised or untreated. 
https://www.bmj.com/content/317/7154/307.long</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000636</IRI>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122</IRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000636</IRI>
        <Literal>A statistic that represents the number of units that needs to be tested to prevent one additional adverse outcome, assuming that positive testing will lead to preventive intervention. The Number Needed to Screen to Prevent is calculated as the Number Needed to Treat divided by the prevalence.

Comment for application: 
The Number Needed to Screen (NNS) value is often rounded up to the next highest whole integer.  The Number Needed to Screen to Detect is distinct from the Number Needed to Screen to Prevent as the formulas to calculate are different, even though both may be abbreviated as NNS.

The formula may be adjusted for test performance characteristics (e.g. dividing by the sensitivity) or assumptions regarding acceptance or adherence of interventions.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000636</IRI>
        <Literal>Expert Working Group Agreement: 2022-08-03 vote 5-0 by Jesus Lopez-Alcalde, Janice Tufte, Eric Harvey, Philippe Rocca-Serra, Harold Lehmann</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000636</IRI>
        <Literal>Brian S. Alper, Harold Lehmann, Joanne Dehnbostel, Kenneth Wilkins, Janice Tufte</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000636</IRI>
        <Literal>NNS</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000636</IRI>
        <Literal>Number needed to screen was then calculated by dividing the number needed to treat for treating risk factors by the prevalence of disease that was unrecognised or untreated. 
https://www.bmj.com/content/317/7154/307.long</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000636</IRI>
        <Literal>number needed to screen to prevent</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000637</IRI>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122</IRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000637</IRI>
        <Literal>A statistic that represents the number of units that needs to be tested to identify one additional case. The Number Needed to Screen to Detect is calculated as the reciprocal of a difference in rate of detected cases with and without screening.

The Number Needed to Screen (NNS) value is often rounded up to the next highest whole integer.  The Number Needed to Screen to Detect is distinct from the Number Needed to Screen to Prevent as the formulas to calculate are different, even though both may be abbreviated as NNS.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000637</IRI>
        <Literal>Expert Working Group Agreement: 2022-08-03 vote 5-0 by Jesus Lopez-Alcalde, Janice Tufte, Eric Harvey, Philippe Rocca-Serra, Harold Lehmann</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000637</IRI>
        <Literal>Brian S. Alper, Harold Lehmann, Joanne Dehnbostel, Kenneth Wilkins, Janice Tufte</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000637</IRI>
        <Literal>NNS</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000637</IRI>
        <Literal>number needed to screen to detect</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000638</IRI>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428</IRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000638</IRI>
        <Literal>A statistic that represents the number of units that, if treated or exposed to the intervention, lead to one additional undesired outcome. The Number Needed to Harm is calculated as the reciprocal of a treatment effect estimate, where the effect estimate is expressed as a risk difference.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000638</IRI>
