        <Literal>percentage</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000640</IRI>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000122</IRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000640</IRI>
        <Literal>The logrank test is a statistical hypothesis test used to compare the survival distributions of two or more groups. It is commonly employed in survival analysis, where the primary interest lies in comparing the survival experiences of different groups over time.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
